    {
      "title": "Start here",
      "slug": "start-here",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 99,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<div class=\"lead\">Welcome, {First}!</div>\r\n\r\n\r\nThis beautiful swirl shawl was inspired by a hand knitting pattern.  Why should hand knitters have all the fun?<br>\r\nIt's a DIY, because you can use any yarn and any machine.  Just a little planning and help with the math and you'll be knitting in no time!<br>\r\n\r\nThis course will walk you through all the planning steps. It shows techniques that may be new to you.<br>If this is your first knitting project or your 100th, follow along, the skills you gain here will be invaluable for future knitting projects.\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\">\r\nIf you are new here, the video below will help you learn to navigate this course so you can get the most benefit from the material that is included.\r\n</blockquote>\r\nPlease take a few minutes and walk through how to access the lessons and get the most out of your course.<br /> <b>Don't skip lessons</b> ... for example, you may feel that you know how to cast on ... but sometimes you will pick up a tip that you can use while watching a video.<br><blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>Another reason to follow the course material in order - Throughout the lessons, you'll be making decisions about your shawlette.  We will record your decisions to create your custom pattern.</em></blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/16/swirl_shawl/swirl1.jpg\">\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 1345,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "221120492",
              "title": "Machine Knitting Courses",
              "legacyComponentId": 1395,
              "order": 3
            }
          ],
          "title": "Start Here",
          "slug": "start-here",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 429,
            "blockType": "Questions"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Originally designed as a 1 skein project (100 grams), you can choose to make your shawlette any size you like.<br>The number of needles available on your machine will determine the largest size. (The bind off edge is the widest point). The length can be adjusted by knitting without shaping at the widest point.<br>Because it is knit from the smallest edge to the widest, you can knit until you run out of needles (or yarn).<br>Using natural fibers, and blocking well, additional finishing is not needed. Although you may want to dress up the edges with crochet for a finishing touch.<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 1462,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<blockquote class=\"blockquote_style\">If you don't yet have a plan ... no problem!  You can enter this information when you create your custom pattern.</blockquote>",
