            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/16/swirl_shawl/compare_edges.png\">\r\n<div class=\"lead\">Does it bother anyone else that the sample shawlette<br> has one decorative edge and one plain edge (the bind off edge)?</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"lead\">A machine-knit sawtooth edge could be the answer!<br></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n       \r\n            <b>To use this edge on the Asymmetric Shawlette:</b></br>\r\n               <ol>\r\n                    <li>Follow the pattern to the bind off edge</li>\r\n                   <li>Scrap off</li>\r\n                  <li>Work one of the edges shown in the video below (or your personal variation), using sew-as-you-go to pick up and finish the live garment stitches</li>\r\n               </ol>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/16/swirl_shawl/sawtooth_intro.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe video below offesr multiple versions of this edge ... consider adding more eyelets for a more lacy look.\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 1466,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859733",
              "title": "Sawtooth Edges on the Machine",
              "legacyComponentId": 1467,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
